                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d6a8429-c03b-32ee-a243-ea9cbfed272f",
                        "entry_id": "69ac5007-a728-3493-bfd2-0d1bb67fceb7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative spelling of mopey."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "50bb3e92-7b4b-48a4-a617-b9a616e2e368",
                                "sense_id": "4d6a8429-c03b-32ee-a243-ea9cbfed272f",
                                "text": "In all those cases where the hog is mopy and chilly looking I would, after the first stage of lowering the pulse has passed, recommend a teacupful of a strong infusion of the leaves of dogwood or the same quantity of a strong cold infusion of boneset."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0003469-fbb2-48bf-9c22-f400487b722c",
                                "sense_id": "4d6a8429-c03b-32ee-a243-ea9cbfed272f",
                                "text": "She's that altered, nothing interests her; and she's so pale and mopy looking, always going down to the cemetery."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2d27604-8c01-421c-b70c-f2a9d15e4058",
                                "sense_id": "4d6a8429-c03b-32ee-a243-ea9cbfed272f",
                                "text": "And because I was so quiet and mopy my stepdaddy Winn would get great kicks out of tickling me till I almost had a spasm."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "602e1a63-c00b-3495-9ed6-dcc44bd381d8",
                "word": "mopy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "bb3342de-ad4e-4221-88ef-a399e3086e19",
                        "entry_id": "602e1a63-c00b-3495-9ed6-dcc44bd381d8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mopies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a6f2be75-afe5-3fd4-9543-d440d9822be0",
                        "entry_id": "602e1a63-c00b-3495-9ed6-dcc44bd381d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One of the multiple original copies printed from a single original."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "43ae0b54-7ec5-47b4-9ae0-08176bdf5ae7",
                                "sense_id": "a6f2be75-afe5-3fd4-9543-d440d9822be0",
                                "text": "Some people value the crisp appearance of mopies or find it time- consuming to operate both printers and copiers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bc264d4-fca0-4ff5-b2ce-ab1e974ad792",
                                "sense_id": "a6f2be75-afe5-3fd4-9543-d440d9822be0",
                                "text": "Hewlett-Packard says that the LaserJet was also the first printer that could print multiple original documents (now known as mopies), and was the first personal laser printer to hit the 1,200-dpi resolution barrier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc285bfd-6d46-42e8-9ec8-c8fda88a0822",
                                "sense_id": "a6f2be75-afe5-3fd4-9543-d440d9822be0",
                                "text": "So printing mopies (multiple original prints) is now a reality."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
